{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JU8sMeqLXi1ScqqehdMPNr","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"timestamp\": \"2026-07-18T03:41:12.000Z\", \"author\": \"coder-sonnet\", \"type\": \"blocked\", \"message\": \"Implemented the INF-001 deliverable in full within src/gas/setup/** (only allowed path, roadmap.md not touched): schema.gs (PANEL_OPS_SCHEMA, 16 tabs with header arrays transcribed field-for-field from data-model.md, in listed order, no extra columns); seeds.gs (WORKFLOW_STATES_SEED = 17 rows transcribed from workflow-state-machine.md's state table; TRANSITION_MATRIX_SEED generated from that doc's Transition Matrix + Guards sections, keyed by from-state with roles/guard per allowed transition, plus lost_from_any_non_terminal and management_reopen per the doc's prose rules; SEQUENCES_SEED as an initial counter shape -- not specified elsewhere, flagged as an implementation choice for INF-002 to confirm/extend; CONFIGURATION_SEED covering all 8 keys named in the ticket with the exact literal values given (vat_rate=0.19, edge_waste_factor=1.10, quotation_validity_hours=48, aging_alert_minutes=60) plus transition_matrix/sequences/empty withholding_rules/empty company_legal_info; LOSS_REASONS_SEED as a generic Spanish starter list -- no canonical list exists anywhere in the repo, ticket explicitly calls for a 'starter list' so this is a placeholder, flagged for later replacement via the Loss_Reasons UI; USERS_SEED as 3 explicit non-functional placeholder emails (management/sales/billing) per the ticket's own wording 'Users placeholders'); setup.gs (setupPanelOpsWorkbook() -- idempotent: stores the created Spreadsheet ID in PropertiesService.getScriptProperties() so re-runs reopen the same workbook instead of creating a duplicate; per-tab header write only happens if the current header row differs from schema; per-tab seeding only happens if the tab has zero data rows, except Configuration which is upserted by key so user edits to e